Subject: [PATCH] vhost-user-bridge: do not advertise unsupported guest announce

VIRTIO_NET_F_GUEST_ANNOUNCE requires VIRTIO_NET_F_CTRL_VQ and a control
virtqueue implementing VIRTIO_NET_CTRL_ANNOUNCE_ACK. The bridge implements
neither. Linux rejects the device when it sees this invalid combination
through UML's direct vhost-user transport.

diff --git a/contrib/vhost-user-bridge/vhost-user-bridge.c b/contrib/vhost-user-bridge/vhost-user-bridge.c
--- a/contrib/vhost-user-bridge/vhost-user-bridge.c
+++ b/contrib/vhost-user-bridge/vhost-user-bridge.c
@@ -460,8 +460,7 @@
 static uint64_t
 vubr_get_features(VuDev *dev)
 {
-    return 1ULL << VIRTIO_NET_F_GUEST_ANNOUNCE |
-        1ULL << VIRTIO_NET_F_MRG_RXBUF |
+    return 1ULL << VIRTIO_NET_F_MRG_RXBUF |
         1ULL << VIRTIO_F_VERSION_1;
 }
 
